      "body": "## Overview\n\nInclude unattempted KV blocks in Mooncake Store load-error reporting when a split read stops early. Otherwise, block-level recomputation can retain an unloaded prefix after TP-rank rotation.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Partial failures invalidate failed blocks and all later, unattempted batches.\n- Exceptions invalidate the current batch and all later batches.\n- Successful loads and local cached blocks are preserved.\n\n## Validation\n\nBase: `7a64fb8fc9239cb65e0df9313fa759594dfb206a`.\n\nRegression: 3 targeted cases fail before the fix due to missing invalid block IDs; all 341 related tests pass after the fix.\nModel validation: Qwen3-0.6B-Base, TP=1, produces identical token IDs before and after the fix across six controlled scenarios covering successful loads, partial failures, and exceptions.\n\n\n## Details\n\nThe receiver rotates aligned keys and block IDs, then batches reads to fit the staging budget. Previously, stopping after a failure reported only failed keys, or only the current batch on an exception. Later batches were never read or marked invalid.\n\nFor example, read order `[2, 0, 1]` can leave block 1 unloaded when block 2 fails. Reporting only block 2 lets recomputation retain the unloaded block 1. Track the number of keys in fully successful batches to include the unread suffix in error reporting. HMA retains its existing request-level failure handling.\n\nAI assistance was used to implement and validate this change.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
